First Author: Gouiaa
Title: Novel dimensionality reduction method, Taelcore, enhances lung transplantation risk prediction
Source number: 17  ￼

Very short summary: This study proposed Taelcore, a topology-preserving autoencoder framework, to improve prediction of acute cellular rejection (ACR) after lung transplantation. Five key findings were: (1) the clinical lung-transplant dataset included 40 patients, of whom 7 (17.5%) developed ACR within 1 year; (2) nine early post-transplant variables were used, including soluble CD31, PaO2/FiO2, and SOFA respiratory scores at 24, 48, and 72 hours; (3) before topological improvement, MLP achieved 80% success and GNB 90%; (4) after topological improvement, Taelcore improved RF from 50% to 80% and MLP from 80% to 90%, while GNB remained 90%; and (5) the latent-space figure showed clearer linear separation of ACR vs non-ACR with Taelcore than with AE, PCA, t-SNE, or UMAP. Tables 1–2 and Figures 1–4 were directly used for this extraction.

